: {value: \"AC or battery\"}? Hmm.\n\nI'll do:\n- power_supply_voltage: {min:100,max:240}, V\n- power_supply_frequency: {min:50,max:60}, Hz\n- power_supply_type: \"AC\"\n- battery_voltage: 3.6, V\n\n- Software identification: Version V2.xx (xx = 01…99) → attribute \"software_identification\" value \"V2.xx\". Also note displayed after pressing (i) key — could be a note; maybe skip or include in description. I'll skip the display note, or include a characteristic \"software_identification_display\": \"displayed after pressing the (i) key\". Probably fine to omit; but \"don't fabricate\" doesn't forbid including. I'll include a note? The schema for footnotes doesn't apply. I'll add it as part of certified_type description? Description is \"free-text description if present\" — the fragment doesn't give a description of the instrument. I'll omit description.\n\nRecommendation: R76, edition 2006, scheme A, accuracy_classes [\"III\", \"IIII\"].\n\nTest reports: id \"NMi-2561497-01\", date 2021-05-04, pages 53, role \"type_evaluation_report\".\n\nRevision history: none.\n\nFootnotes: none (the parenthetical isn't a footnote).\n\nIssuing authority: name \"NMi\" — include; maybe also oiml_issuer_id null omitted. member_state \"The Netherlands\".\n\ncertificate.number: \"R76/2006-A-NL1-21.15\". page_total: not present. date_issued: not present. oiml_issuer_id: not present.\n\nmodel_family: not present (single indicator) — omit.\n\nValues must be structured objects with value/unit_symbol/unit_id. So each type_level entry: {\"maximum_capacity\": ...} shape: `<label>: {value, unit_symbol, unit_id, footnote_markers[]}`.\n\nLet me format type_level:\n\n```\n\"accuracy_class\": {\"value\": \"III or IIII\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null}\n```\n\nHmm, but recommendation.accuracy_classes covers it. I could omit accuracy_class from characteristics? The characteristics table lists it. I'll keep both.\n\n- \"weighing_ranges\": {\"value\": \"Single interval or multi-interval\"}\